<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shindongbang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>Shindongbang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Shindongbang Corp bought 35,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 soybean at mixed basis prices over September and November futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a senior official of the company said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The official said the shipment was set for early October from the U.S. Gulf. Arrival was slated for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>He said the purchasing price was between $325 and $330 per tonne, C&amp;F, from a U.S. grain exporter.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
